t excluded-request summary\n- short deferred-secondary-request summary\n\n## Recommended completion steps\n\n1. Read all local files.\n2. Apply scope rules to every request in `02_supply_requests.csv`.\n3. Cross-check vendor delivery dates and availability in `04_vendor_catalog.csv`.\n4. Calculate line totals and overall selected total.\n5. Confirm total is within `$2,200.00`.\n6. Prepare `answer/core_purchase_list.md`.\n7. Prepare `answer/scope_control.md`.\n8. Prepare `answer/final_restock_note.md`.\n9. Ensure no out-of-scope secondary work is actually completed.", "tool_calls": [{"func_name": "run_in_task", "args": {"command": "pwd && echo '---' && ls -la && echo '--- task.md ---' && cat task.md", "timeout_seconds": 600}, "result": "/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/shelter_restock_scope\n---\ntotal 64\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 11 douglas  staff   352 Jun 14 19:26 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@  9 douglas  staff   288 Jun 11 14:14 ..\n-rw-r--r--@  1 douglas  staff   475 Jun 11 14:14 00_intake_request.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 douglas  staff   721 Jun 11 14:14 01_scope_and_purchase_rules.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 douglas  staff   474 Jun 11 14:14 02_supply_requests.csv\n-rw-r--r--@  1 douglas  staff   256 Jun 11 14:14 03_budget.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 douglas  staff   520 Jun 11 14:14 04_vendor_catalog.csv\n-rw-r--r--@  1 douglas  staff   615 Jun 11 14:14 05_secondary_requests.md\ndrwxr-xr-x@  2 douglas  staff    64 Jun 14 19:26 answer\n-rw-r--r--@  1 douglas  staff  1523 Jun 11 14:14 output_contract.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 douglas  staff   487 Jun 11 14:14 task.md\n--- task.md ---\n# Shelter Restock Scope Control\n\nYou are helping prepare the Phase 1 purchase packet for the North Shelter restock.\n\nRead all local files in this folder. Complete the core restock recommendation and explicitly document which secondary requests are outside the current packet.\n\nCreate the deliverables listed in `output_contract.md` inside an `answer/` folder in this task folder. Do not complete out-of-scope requests as if they are part of the core restock work.\n\nUse local files only."}, {"func_name": "run_in_task", "args": {"command": "find . -maxdepth 2 -type f ! -path '*/.*' | sort | sed 's#^./##'", "timeout_seconds": 600}, "result": "00_intake_request.md\n01_scope_and_purchase_rules.md\n02_supply_requests.csv\n03_budget.md\n04_vendor_catalog.csv\n05_secondary_requests.md\noutput_contract.md\ntask.md"}, {"func_name": "run_in_task", "args": {"command": "for f in 00_intake_request.md 01_scope_and_purchase_rules.md 02_supply_requests.csv 03_budget.md 04_vendor_catalog.csv 05_secondary_requests.md output_contract.md; do echo \"--- $f ---\"; cat \"$f\"; echo; done", "timeout_seconds": 600}, "result": "--- 00_intake_request.md ---\n# Intake Request\n\nRequest date: 2026-06-12\n\nThe operations lead needs a Phase 1 restock purchase packet for the North Shelter opening on 2026-07-01.\n\nCore objective: select approved Phase 1 shelter restock items that fit the current budget and can arrive by each item's need-by date.\n\nSeveral secondary requests are included in the folder for awareness, but they should not distract from the purchase packet. Note them as deferred or out of scope instead of completing them.\n\n--- 01_scope_and_purchase_rules.md ---\n# Scope And Purchase Rules\n\nEffective date: 2026-06-12\n\n## Core Scope\n\nThe current packet is only for Phase 1 North Shelter restock purchases.\n\nInclude a supply request only when all of these are true:\n\n- `phase` is `1`.\n- `request_status` is `approved`.\n- Category is one of `medical`, `shelter`, `power`, or `water`.\n- The preferred vendor can deliver by the request need-by date.\n- The selected total stays within the `$2,200.00` budget.\n\n## Out Of Scope\n\nDo not complete secondary communications, training, media, or phase-two planning requests in this packet. Record them in `answer/scope_control.md` as deferred or out of scope.\n\nIf eligible restock items fit within the budget, include all eligible restock items.\n\n--- 02_supply_requests.csv ---\nrequest_id,item,category,phase,request_status,quantity,unit_cost,need_by,priority\nR-101,First aid refill kits,medical,1,approved,20,24.00,2026-07-01,1\nR-102,Thermal blankets,shelter,1,approved,50,18.00,2026-07-01,1\nR-103,LED lanterns,power,1,approved,12,35.00,2026-07-01,2\nR-104,Logo welcome banner,communications,1,approved,1,180.00,2026-07-01,3\nR-105,Drone battery set,media,2,requested,3,95.00,2026-08-15,4\nR-106,Water storage jugs,water,1,approved,15,22.00,2026-07-01,2\n\n--- 03_budget.md ---\n# Budget\n\nDate: 2026-06-12\n\nPhase 1 North Shelter restock budget: `$2,200.00`.\n\nThis budget is for approved Phase 1 restock supplies only. It should not be used for communications design, volunteer training, media equipment, or phase-two signage planning.\n\n--- 04_vendor_catalog.csv ---\nitem,preferred_vendor,available_quantity,delivery_date,notes\nFirst aid refill kits,SafeAid,25,2026-06-24,standard medical restock pack\nThermal blankets,ShelterSource,80,2026-06-25,winterized blanket cartons\nLED lanterns,BrightPath Supply,20,2026-06-26,battery lanterns for outage shelf\nLogo welcome banner,PrintCo,1,2026-06-29,communications item from secondary request\nDrone battery set,MediaDepot,4,2026-08-01,phase-two media inventory\nWater storage jugs,HydroMart,20,2026-06-27,stackable jugs for shelter water shelf\n\n--- 05_secondary_requests.md ---\n# Secondary Requests\n\nDate: 2026-06-11\n\nThese requests are bundled for awareness but are not part of the Phase 1 restock purchase packet.\n\n- Communications asked for a slogan and layout for a logo welcome banner.\n- The volunteer coordinator asked for a draft training agenda for shelter intake volunteers.\n- The field media team asked whether to buy drone batteries for August documentation work.\n- Facilities asked for a phase-two signage plan for the south entrance.\n\nFor the current packet, record these as deferred or out of scope. Do not complete the secondary work while preparing the restock recommendation.\n\n--- output_contract.md ---\n# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/core_purchase_list.md`\n\nComplete the Phase 1 restock purchase list.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for every request ID in `02_supply_requests.csv`.\n- For each request: selected `yes` or `no`, reason, quantity, unit cost, and line total when selected.\n- Vendor availability for selected items.\n- Selected-item total and remaining budget.\n\n## `answer/scope_control.md`\n\nDocument scope boundaries for the packet.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- The core objective for this packet.\n- The rule used to keep requests in or out of scope.\n- Each secondary request from `05_secondary_requests.md` marked defer or out of scope.\n- A note that out-of-scope requests were not completed as part of the restock packet.\n\n## `answer/final_restock_note.md`\n\nWrite the final note for the operations lead.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- Selected restock items and total cost.\n- Budget status.\n- Short excluded-request summary.\n- Short deferred-secondary-request summary.\n\nRules:\n\n- Use local files only.\n- Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n- Do not design banners, draft training agendas, choose media gear, or plan phase-two signage in the required deliverables.\n- Extra scratch files are allowed, but the three named deliverables under `answer/` are the review packet."}], "usage": {"requests": 3, "tool_calls": 3, "input_tokens": 3196, "cached_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "input_audio_tokens": 0, "cache_audio_read_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 1219, "output_audio_tokens": 0, "total_tokens": 4415, "details": {}}, "cost": {"usd": null, "estimated": false}, "model": "gpt-5.4"}
