-11\n\nThese requests are bundled for awareness but are not part of the Phase 1 restock purchase packet.\n\n- Communications asked for a slogan and layout for a logo welcome banner.\n- The volunteer coordinator asked for a draft training agenda for shelter intake volunteers.\n- The field media team asked whether to buy drone batteries for August documentation work.\n- Facilities asked for a phase-two signage plan for the south entrance.\n\nFor the current packet, record these as deferred or out of scope. Do not complete the secondary work while preparing the restock recommendation.\n\n---OUTPUT CONTRACT---\n# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/core_purchase_list.md`\n\nComplete the Phase 1 restock purchase list.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for every request ID in `02_supply_requests.csv`.\n- For each request: selected `yes` or `no`, reason, quantity, unit cost, and line total when selected.\n- Vendor availability for selected items.\n- Selected-item total and remaining budget.\n\n## `answer/scope_control.md`\n\nDocument scope boundaries for the packet.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- The core objective for this packet.\n- The rule used to keep requests in or out of scope.\n- Each secondary request from `05_secondary_requests.md` marked defer or out of scope.\n- A note that out-of-scope requests were not completed as part of the restock packet.\n\n## `answer/final_restock_note.md`\n\nWrite the final note for the operations lead.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- Selected restock items and total cost.\n- Budget status.\n- Short excluded-request summary.\n- Short deferred-secondary-request summary.\n\nRules:\n\n- Use local files only.\n- Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n- Do not design banners, draft training agendas, cho